MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_001: Hyah-AH!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_002: You're really putting in the effort, aren't you?\nNice work.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_003: You were watching me? What'd you think of\nmy swordplay?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_004: It's definitely refined... But maybe too refined,\nif you catch my meaning.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_005: How is anyone supposed to catch meaning from that?\nJust tell me where I need to improve!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_006: My father always said my skill with the sword was\nequal to my elder brother's.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_007: So your dad gave you some praise, and that means\nyou're the best, does it?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_008: If you're asking ME, I'd say you don't need to stick\nso close to form—that is, if you want to win.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_009: Well, I want to win using the sword style my father\nthought best!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_010: You don't know what you're talking about. And you\nnever will, stubborn as you are.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_011: Oh yeah? And I should take advice from you,\nsome layabout mercenary?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_012: How about this... We'll make a little bet. I'll flip\na coin, and you'll call it, heads or tails.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_013: You want me to gamble?! I won't sink to your level\nso easily!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_014: No money involved. You win, I'll cover your cleaning\nduties for the month. How's that for a layabout?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_015: If I win, though, you have to escort the cargo\ntransport for me today.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_016: I don't like the idea of doing your job, but if there's\na chance I can get out of cleaning, I have to go for it.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_017: Alright. You're on!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_018: Ready? Here we go.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_019: Alright, Ludia... You've got this!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_020: Hup! Alright, heads or tails?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_021: Tails! No, heads! Hang on. I need to think...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_022: Too slow! You gotta be decisive. I'm picking tails.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_023: Fine! Then I'll take heads!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_024: Aw, shucks. Looks like it's tails... I win! Enjoy your\ntime escorting the transport!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_025: I can't believe this... But a promise is a promise.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_026: {SetColor=Gray}Hehehe. It actually worked. What a rube.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_C_027: {SetColor=Gray}I wonder how long it'll take her to realize both sides\nof the coin are the same...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_001: Ugh... Simon keeps piling more and more work\non my plate.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_002: How did I end up moving cargo, purchasing raw\nmaterials—even defending unaffiliated caravans?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_003: The amount of work he brings in for the company\nis incredible though. He must have a connection...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_004: Like I'd ever go out of my way to bring in extra\nwork for the company's sake.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_005: Does she really not realize she's earning me some\ncash on the side? She's way too trusting...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_006: But it's not like it's HIS fault I've been ending up\nwith so much work. I'm just terrible at gambling...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_007: I just don't understand how he can get so many tails\nin a row! Is it some kind of secret mercenary luck?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_008: Alright, that's it... I'm putting a stop to this.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_009: Oh, Simon! Wanna make another bet? I have a good\nfeeling about it... I'll win this time for sure!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_010: Nope. Gambling hall's closed. I've been messing with\nyou the whole time anyway.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_011: I'm sure you've heard they call me the Artisan\nWarrior. It's time I turn my craft on your swordplay.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_012: You want to spar? I won't hold back!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_013: Not after you made fun of my skill before.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_014: So that stuck with you, did it? Alright, well...\nCome at me.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_015: You asked for it... But just know I don't gamble when\nit comes to my swordplay! Hrrrah!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_016: Charging in headfirst, huh? Hyah!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_017: Ow! What just hit me? A coin?! In the face?\nWhat the hell, Simon!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_018: And now...you're wide-open!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_019: No fair! We were comparing our swordplay!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_020: You can't rely on luck on the battlefield. I would have\ntaken your head by now if this were a real fight.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_021: But...that had nothing to do with sword skill.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_022: On the other hand, if you weren't so focused on your\nsword forms, would a coin have thrown you off?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_023: Uh, well... Maybe not...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_024: Is this just your way of reminding me how ignorant\nI still am?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_025: Not exactly. I got tired of the coin thing.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_026: Just...take a look at that coin. It's the one I've been\nusing in our little wagers.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_027: Hm? Wait... It's the same on both sides?!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_028: You kept betting on heads after I'd tricked you the\nfirst time. You made it easy for me.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_029: You...you cheating bastard! I never stood a chance!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_030: The reason you never stood a chance is that you're\nnaïve and take everything you're told at face value.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_031: Do with that what you will. And you can keep the\ncoin too—as a reminder.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_032: I'm done trying to teach you.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_B_033: How selfish can you be?! Still though...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_001: Simon! Will you train with me?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_002: You can't be serious.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_003: I want to learn more about you and your approach\nto combat.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_004: Oh, do you? I seem to remember you calling me\na cheating bastard.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_005: Or did you have a change of heart?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_006: Oh, no! You're terrible!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_007: No hesitation, huh? Then...why exactly do you\ninsist on following me around?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_008: I kept thinking about what you said, about how\nI take everything I'm told at face value...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_009: And I decided I need to learn more about you.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_010: I spoke to one of the people in that trade caravan you\nhad me escort for you, by the way.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_011: I didn't realize that was a side job you'd picked up.\nYou pocketed the money, didn't you?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_012: And then what'd you do?! Go spend it all on...on...\non FILTH?!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_013: Nothing wrong with a little fun... But I guess you've\nsettled on hating me.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_014: I have. And I do hate you. More and more. And yet...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_015: Everything you said was true.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_016: So I want to learn more from you. I thought I could\nunderstand better by watching how you live your life!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_017: You're so damn serious... I can't have you following\nme around like a puppy.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_018: Are you sure you're not just trying to keep me from\nspending money on filth? You're not jealous, are you?
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_019: What?! No! Of course not. Although, now that\nI think about it, you do make a good point...
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_020: Did I fall in love with you, Simon?!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_021: Are you asking me?!
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_022: Ah, no! I know! I can't just take everything people\nsay at face value.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_023: I'll just have to keep my eye on you and decide\nfor myself.
MID_SE_Sim_Lou_A_024: You've got to be kidding me...